"Rapport III is a knights' Privately Governed Territory of river country, fields and docks."
"Knights of the und'h family live there, and Esh-erdi and Lind-otta keep a house there."
"The city of Wathe lies nearby, known for revelers' nights."
"Its river summonarium is a pavilion roofed over the water, its floor edged in orange light."
"The Pitcherhouse on Wathe's Ribbon is a casual riverside pavilion serving bundlefruit wine."
"Squat cylindrical apartments of glossy sculpted mud are kept ready for anyone to use."
"Esh-erdi's river community links houses by shared rooms and walkways; open doors welcome all."
"Votaries tend a garden of high-maintenance ingredients near Esh-erdi's house."
"Alden's birth tree, a Tennessee honey locust, grows there in a climate pocket set to January."
"Woven-grass seating circles lit by carved gourd lanterns sit in a copse along a long trail."
"A yatanger triangle, a raised platform on a grassy mound, is used for brewing magic."
"Its training fields host days-long simulated battles against chaos for young knights."
"A rock teacher's house on the river has a lawn of more than a hundred giant specimen rocks."
"Young knights hosted a picnic there for declared candidates."
